:2,"numoutlets":1,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-11","maxclass":"comment","text":"Unlike lists, however, dictionaries are passed by reference.  The result is that if you do not use the dictionary immediately, the values collected in the dictionary might be cleared before you actually get around to using them!","rect":[10,120,490,50],"patchingRect":[10,120,490,50],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"linecount":3},{"id":"obj-1","maxclass":"comment","text":"The dict.group object functions for dictionaries like the zl.group object does for lists.\nThis means that as soon as the dictionary is sent forward, the dictionary is then cleared so that the process can begin over again.","rect":[10,65,490,50],"patchingRect":[10,65,490,50],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"linecount":3},{"id":"obj-15","maxclass":"comment","text":"The solution is to insert a dict object afterwards.  This will clone (make a copy of) the dictionary prior to its being cleared.","rect":[10,175,500,36],"patchingRect":[10,175,500,36],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"linecount":2},{"id":"obj-38","maxclass":"panel","text":"","rect":[272,424,165,55],"patchingRect":[272,424,165,55],"border":1,"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0},{"id":"obj-37","maxclass":"panel","text":"","rect":[97,424,165,55],"patchingRect":[97,424,165,55],"border":1,"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0}],"lines":[{"id":"pline-0","sourceId":"obj-19","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-20","targetInlet":0,"midpoints":[271.5,318,271.5,318]},{"id":"pline-1","sourceId":"obj-20","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-21","targetInlet":0,"midpoints":[271.5,357,412.5,357]},{"id":"pline-2","sourceId":"obj-20","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-34","targetInlet":1,"midpoints":[271.5,384,237.5,384]},{"id":"pline-3","sourceId":"obj-21","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-36","targetInlet":1,"midpoints":[412.5,387,412.5,387]},{"id":"pline-4","sourceId":"obj-25","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-32","targetInlet":0,"midpoints":[111.5,252,111.5,252]},{"id":"pline-5","sourceId":"obj